Optional clean HTML output (added 2026-10-05)
-------------------------------------------

 ./ccv2html --clean CCV.xml cleaned.html

Removes the Personal Information section while retaining the name in
the CV title. Removes fields without text or reference-table values,
including empty language variants. A blank Organization is filled from
Other Organization in the same record, and the consumed Other
Organization field is omitted to avoid duplication. Existing populated
Organization fields are retained. Input XML is never modified.
Without --clean, the existing conversion behavior is retained.

Non-academic work experience (modified 2026-10-05)
------------------------------------------------

Roles display position title, employer and division, dates and status,
then the work description. HTML preserves description line breaks.
Source order and date precision are retained; a missing end date is not
assumed to mean Present. Applies with and without --clean.

Academic employment and affiliations also include their populated Work
Description and Activity Description fields beneath the corresponding
entries (modified 2026-10-05). Blank descriptions are omitted.

Community and Volunteer Activities use the same resume-style layout:
role, organization, dates, then Activity Description, with HTML line
breaks preserved (modified 2026-10-05). Source order is retained and
missing end dates are not inferred. Works with and without --clean.

Theses and Dissertations (modified 2026-10-05)
-------------------------------------------

Both legacy Dissertations and current Thesis/Dissertation XML sections
use a dedicated layout: title, degree, university/location, completion
year/date, then all other populated fields. Includes supervisor, page
count, descriptions, URL, DOI and contribution details when provided.
Blank fields are omitted in this section regardless of --clean.
Distinct populated translations are retained without duplicating the
primary description. Organization reference-table attributes are read
correctly. Applies to HTML and LaTeX output.
